# 0024 XeGfxAccel: ordered deferred flip, Tile4 scanout, page-off device caches, per-frame timeline
#
# Base:  kexts/NVRM/accel after 0002 + 0009 + 0012
# Files: kexts/NVRM/accel/nvrm-accel.cpp, kexts/NVRM/accel/xegfx_accel_names.h
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0024-accel-deferred-flip-tile4-pageoff.patch
#
# Deferred flip (K9 worker of 0012):
#   - flips are ordered after WindowServer's own composite: the plugin marks each surface pending at commit and
#     ready when the GPU finished it (DRM client selector 1); the worker waits for that mark only (markonly), with
#     a fence snapshot / GT-idle poll as fallback; a GPU still busy after iop_xe_idle_ms (default 120) arms anyway
#     and no longer switches deferral off; the stuck-transaction escape completes the transaction without
#     disabling deferral; E2 early signal (before the latch) is off by default (WindowServer double-buffers)
#   - a joined pipe B follows each flip (core's xgJoinerInfo, re-read at the first present after a boot mode)
#   - start no longer reads NVRM's nullmoth-nv-starts boot guard (an NVIDIA counter; -nvoff and nullmoth-remove
#     still stop it); boot-arm waits for the family pipe in flight instead of creating a second one
# Tile4 scanout: DRM client selector 2 takes each WindowServer surface's layout and replies whether Tile4 is on
#   and the surface is scanned out; the plane follows the frame's layout (core's xg_display_kms_plane_layout).
#   On by default; boot argument xegfxtile4=0 starts with it off; debug.xegfxaccel_iop_xe_tile4 switches at run
#   time; more than 20 layout switches in 10 s turn it off.
# Page-off (Apple's IOSurface device-cache model): selectors 5-8 (current / wait for a request / done / detach,
#   WindowServer only) hang an IOSurfaceDeviceCache of the accel's on each surface the plugin keeps a private
#   (Tile4, CCS-compressed) copy of.  A CPU lock calls its control function (op 0): the surface's committed
#   composites are waited for and the plugin's page-off thread copies the copy back to the pages (300 ms at
#   most); a flip or copy of the surface does the same (50 ms).  No current mark is taken while the surface is
#   held locked (IOSurface +0x228 read-only / +0x22c write lock counts, macOS 25G241): WindowServer locks
#   screenshot surfaces before drawing them and reads them under that lock.  debug.nvaccel_iop_xe_po.
# Diagnostics: selector 3 (a surface's lock/unlock seeds), selector 4 (a device-cache probe), debug.nvaccel_iop_xe_locks
#   (CPU locks of WindowServer's drawn surfaces), debug.nvaccel_iop_xe_tl (the last 200 flips: queued, worker
#   pickup, composite done, arm, latch, signal, turnaround in us).
# Status: in daily use with the 0026 plugin.
#
