+// sequence of the plugin's page-off thread.  A CPU lock of the surface calls nvXePoControl op 0 in the locking thread:
+// this surface's committed GPU writes are waited for (its marks), a request is queued for the page-off thread, and the
+// lock waits for it (300 ms at most; then the pages keep their last linear content -- old, never Tile4).  The flip
+// worker does the same before it scans a surface whose copy is current.
